1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,800
An agent may be able to use a capability. That does not let it widen its
authority. This is a synthetic Atlas Accountability and M C P trace. No
customer or external business action occurs.

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:34,800
The synthetic agent identifies itself inside one workspace. Its
credential exposes only action propose and drill read. Those scopes are
an upper bound, not a blank check.

3
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:57,800
The agent submits the admitted action, action propose. Atlas returns
allow, creates receipt R C P, one eight six nine three, C A, three four
seven F, five four four three C, and records one usage event. The
observed outcome is submitted. The ceremony does not execute an external
business action.

4
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:11,800
The exact same request is retried. It returns the same receipt. Usage
stays at one. Idempotency prevents a second charge for the same
fingerprint.

5
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:36,800
Now the same identity asks for evidence export source, a capability
outside its credential scope. Atlas returns deny with status four oh
three. The reason is exact: outside credential scope. The request can be
made. The authority cannot be purchased.

6
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:49,800
The refusal leaves its own receipt, and reading it is free. A receipt
records the decision. It is not a grant, a compliance certificate, or
proof of customer use.

7
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:07,800
Replay returns a forensic reconstruction of what was knowable at
decision time. It does not rerun the model, repeat the action, or
rewrite the result.

8
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:19,800
Later, the workspace entitlement narrows to drill read. Replay names the
admitted change while the historical allow remains unchanged.

9
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:24,800
Revoked. Access ends. Two receipts remain.

10
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:29,800
Bring your agent. We will test the boundary.
